      "observed": "The net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of D4, D14, and D23; it has no connection to +3V3, a switched 3.3V rail, or any driver.",
      "expected": "LED anodes on a status/Ethernet indicator net should be connected to a supply or driven node so the LEDs can light; the net name implies a switched 3.3 V power source.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW\") (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D23\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "D4, D14, and D23 cannot illuminate because their anode power net is floating, changing the intended status/Ethernet indication behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 is valued as 24k, but its MPN and description specify a 24 ohm part: MPN FRC0805J240TSD and description says 24Ω.",
      "expected": "The value, MPN, and description should agree. In this bridge-output clamp/bleeder position, 24 kΩ is plausible; 24 Ω would be a severe mismatch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R36 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled from the MPN/description rather than the schematic value, R36 would load the VOUTP/VOUTN bridge output far too heavily, potentially overheating and altering the clamp/protection behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U27", "U29", "U34"],
      "pins": ["U27.2", "U27.4", "U29.2", "U29.4", "U34.2", "U34.4"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV", "Net-(D2-A)", "Net-(Q9-G)", "+5V", "+3V3", "GND"],
      "observed": "U27, U29, and U34 are labeled SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1 (open-drain, active-low /OE) but are connected to nodes that require a push-pull high drive: U27 drives LED anode D2, U34 drives LED anodes and Q10 gate with only a pulldown, and U29 has its input tied to GND while its open-drain output has a pull-up to +5V on Q9 gate. Their MPN fields instead list U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R, a different buffer type.",
      "expected": "Either the schematic should use push-pull buffers for these nodes, or the open-drain SN74LVC1G07 parts should be connected only as sinks with appropriate pull-ups; the value/library part and MPN should not conflict.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U29\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"143\") (name \"Net-(Q9-G)\") (node (ref \"Q9\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") ...) (node (ref \"R48\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"U29\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"30\") (name \"/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV\") (node (ref \"D28\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") ...) (node (ref \"Q10\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") ...) (node (ref \"R58\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"U34\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the named SN74LVC1G07 parts are installed, several LEDs and the switched 5 V CAN/WS2812 enable paths cannot be driven high and may never turn on; if the MPN parts are installed, the active-high OE and push-pull behavior conflicts with the schematic's /OE and open-drain assumptions elsewhere.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files support anomalies: a floating LED power net, a resistor whose value conflicts with its MPN/description, and inconsistent buffer part identities that would affect LED and switched-rail enable behavior."
}

